    "biography": "<p>@UUID[JournalEntry.azX1hjbc0PUp2AA2.JournalEntryPage.Dy9L39SvdB7rns0t]{Profile: The Moles}</p><blockquote><p><em>Everything&#39;s for sale down below.</em></p></blockquote><table class=\"sbn-ficha\"><tbody><tr><th>Type</th><td>Brokers</td></tr><tr><th>Domain</th><td>The Sealed Underground</td></tr><tr><th>Location</th><td>@UUID[JournalEntry.jg1zpvYlDFMJRY8Q]{The Sealed Underground (Seattle Underground)}</td></tr><tr><th>Members</th><td>@UUID[JournalEntry.dj4gIszHHTN1QRKk]{Abel Thornquist}, @UUID[JournalEntry.PBJeE9T9n0BjB6ag]{Ezra “Static” Lund}, @UUID[JournalEntry.BRQMU0Tf8VSNaZ5o]{Jun Takeda}</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The brokers of the Seattle Underground: the stone of 1889 and the cables of 2026.</p><h3>Domain</h3><ul><li><strong>Chasse 2:</strong> homeless people, in exchange for shelter</li><li><strong>Lien 3:</strong> doormen, cleaners, and technicians all over the city</li><li><strong>Portillon 5:</strong> nobody enters the Sealed Underground without Thornquist knowing</li></ul>",
